From 94812b1d160a45cad0310166b395d74283118fce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mayor <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 22:11:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 59/66] fix(witness): auto-reap SAFE_TO_NUKE polecats under
 capacity pressure (feryn-355z)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a burst of quick completions, town-wide capacity could saturate (0 free
of 11, recovery: 11) and block review/merge dispatch until an operator ran
`gt polecat check-recovery` + `gt polecat nuke` by hand. Completed polecats hold
a slot as idle-recovery-needed (NEEDS_RECOVERY counts toward capacity) when a
stale cleanup_status lags behind their real merged/submitted state, and truly
SAFE_TO_NUKE polecats weren't auto-reaped.

Add a capacity-pressure reap pass to `gt patrol scan` (run each witness patrol)
that automates exactly the operator's manual steps via the same safety-gated
primitives:

  - Pressure-gated: no-op unless the scheduler is genuinely starved (active, 0
    free slots, ready beads queued). With spare capacity it leaves completed
    polecats as reusable-idle, preserving the persistent-polecat reuse model
    (gt-4ac) — reuse is never traded away for nothing.
  - Classifies each idle polecat via check-recovery --reconcile-cleanup, which
    clears a stale cleanup_status only when live predicates prove no work is at
    risk. Live/working sessions are skipped outright.
  - Reaps only SAFE_TO_NUKE-verdict polecats through NukePolecat, which refuses
    when a Mayor ACP session is active (gt-qnp) or an MR is pending in the
    refinery (gt-6a9d), and gt polecat nuke re-checks safety. Recoverable work is
    never reaped — this complements the restart-first zombie policy (gt-dsgp),
    it does not override it.
  - Bounded: reaps at most queued_ready polecats — just enough to clear the
    immediate backlog.
  - Kill switch: GT_WITNESS_DISABLE_AUTOREAP=1 disables it without a redeploy.

Reap outcome is surfaced in `gt patrol scan` (human + --json). Tests cover the
pressure gate matrix, queue-bounded reaping, never-reap-recoverable, no-op
without pressure, and the kill switch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
